# Example: string length, concat, and substring

`length()` is a method; Haxe exposes length as a property. `concat` joins a string with a string or number. `substring(start, end)` is a half-open range; a bad range fails at runtime.

## Schema

```
Player = String/name Int/score
```

## Construction

```
[:Player "Ada" 3]
```

## Methods

```
Player::nameLen = { name.length() }

Player::tag = { name.concat(":").concat(score) }

Player::initial = { name.substring(0, 1) }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var assemblage = PlayerAssemblage.factory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("nameLen");
    trace(assemblage.nameLen());
    trace("tag");
    trace(assemblage.tag());
    trace("initial");
    trace(assemblage.initial());
}
```
